      "rev_n_1_b8988e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_b8988e_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_b8988e",
        "thought_text": "Model the woods as a directed graph where nodes are clearings and edges are paths.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794532793.629662
      },
      "rev_n_2_1e37a0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_1e37a0_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_1e37a0",
        "thought_text": "Use Markov chain analysis to calculate the expected time to reach the exit from any given clearing.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794532793.629676
      },
      "rev_n_3_265f31_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_265f31_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_265f31",
        "thought_text": "Implement a breadth-first search to find the shortest path to the exit and use it to estimate the average time.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794532793.6296833
      },
      "rev_n_1_b8988e_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_b8988e_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_b8988e",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is flawed because it doesn't correctly model the random walk in the woods. Instead of considering all possible paths and their probabilities, it should use a Markov chain approach to calculate the expected time.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_b8988e_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_3d300f607f",
        "created_at": 1794532823.4041033
      },
      "rev_n_2_1e37a0_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_1e37a0_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_1e37a0",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error occurs because we're not handling the case where a node has no neighbors (i.e., it's not connected to any other nodes). Let's modify our approach to handle this case explicitly. Instead of setting the exit probability to 1 for nodes with no neighbors, we should treat them as absorbing states. This will ensure that our Markov chain is properly constructed and solvable.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_1e37a0_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2b5ea5891a",
        "created_at": 1794532934.2952838
      },
      "rev_n_3_265f31_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_265f31_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_265f31",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach incorrectly focused on finding the shortest path using BFS, which is not relevant for calculating the expected time to exit. Instead, we should use a random walk model to estimate the average time, considering all possible paths and their probabilities.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_265f31_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_b75109cb98",
        "created_at": 1794532967.7887733
      },
      "rev_n_4_93ff1e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_93ff1e_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_93ff1e",
        "thought_text": "Model the woods as a Markov chain where each state is a clearing and transitions represent possible moves.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6025528221908898748",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794532979.6994562
      },
      "rev_n_5_5147a5_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_5147a5_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_5147a5",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the transition probabilities between clearings based on the given paths.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6025528221908898748",
